<<<grammar
test/suite/family/fixtures/deep-first-set.scm
<<<input
a
<<<assert
exit 0
# Source is (choice Chain0 (seq B)). Predicting the first alternative resolves
# Chain0's FIRST set, which chains 100 rules deep (Chain0 -> Chain1 -> ... ->
# Chain100 -> token A) before bottoming out. The resolving FIRST-set walk grows
# its `visiting' stack past the old fixed depth of 64 rather than bailing, so the
# deeply-nested alternative is still predicted and the input parses to the bottom
# of the chain. A 100-deep chain would have overflowed (or silently disabled
# pruning at) the old stack[64].
out-contains Chain0
out-contains Chain100
out-contains A
